    "markdown": "**Top of mind:** RL environments are now the training-data sector's main procurement battleground: Anthropic has internally discussed spending over $1B/year on them, Mercor just folded in its July acquisition of simulator startup Deeptune, and a new Menlo Ventures landscape pegs 28 data startups at ~$8.5B combined revenue and ~$100B valuation. Static annotation is being commoditized while environments and real-world workflow data absorb the margin — a direct strategy signal for anyone selling labeling capacity.\n\n## Competitor moves\n\n- **New sector map: 28 training-data startups ≈ $8.5B combined revenue, near-$100B valuation.** Per a Menlo Ventures (Deedy) landscape covered July 24, the Big Four — Scale AI, Surge AI, Mercor, Handshake — hold over three-quarters of revenue and are diverging: Scale into govt/enterprise AI apps (~$200M ARR line), Surge into boutique RLHF ($1.2B revenue with 110 staff), Mercor into expert networks, Handshake into data pipelines. Pure annotation is explicitly called the thinnest-margin link. [BigGo Finance](https://finance.biggo.com/news/99fca087-237a-48f3-ab02-30289cb7d364)\n- **Mercor pushes deeper into RL environments after its July Deeptune acquisition; ARR past $2B.** Deeptune replicates Excel, Salesforce, Slack and Zendesk as sandboxes, and Mercor targets tens of millions in environment ARR by September; Forbes earlier reported talks to raise $500M at a $20B valuation. The fastest-scaling direct competitor for expert-data and environments work. [BigGo Finance](https://finance.biggo.com/news/99fca087-237a-48f3-ab02-30289cb7d364), [Forbes](https://www.forbes.com/sites/richardnieva/2026/07/09/mercor-fundraise/)\n- **Handshake is buying real workflow data straight from enterprises.** Its Employer Data Program plus freelancer uploads of native Word/Excel/code files position it as the pipeline for \"Type 1\" real-work data that labs now prize over made-to-order annotation — annualized gross revenue reached ~$1.1B by April. Pressure point for classic annotation vendors. [BigGo Finance](https://finance.biggo.com/news/99fca087-237a-48f3-ab02-30289cb7d364), [Sacra via AI-Native GTM](https://ainativegtm.substack.com/p/how-handshake-reinvented-itself-for)\n\n## New projects & opportunities\n\n- **RL environments are the biggest open procurement lane.** Anthropic leaders have discussed >$1B/year on environments; OpenAI reportedly pays ~$20K per website environment for its \"UI Gym\" and has bought hundreds. Indian teams with strong SWE/QA benches can build and maintain environments at highly competitive cost. [BigGo Finance](https://finance.biggo.com/news/99fca087-237a-48f3-ab02-30289cb7d364), [SemiAnalysis](https://newsletter.semianalysis.com/p/rl-environments-and-rl-for-science), [Towards AI](https://pub.towardsai.net/why-rl-environments-became-ais-hottest-bottleneck-in-2026-0eec9c15e1bf)\n- **Robotics data demand set to climb: DeepMind shipped Gemini Robotics 2 on July 30.** Whole-body humanoid control plus adaptation to new robot bodies \"within hours\" implies heavy demand for embodied/teleop datasets — the egocentric-video collection work already running in India scales directly with this. [Google DeepMind](https://deepmind.google/blog/gemini-robotics-2-brings-whole-body-intelligence-to-robots/)\n- **Third-party evaluation infrastructure is being institutionalized.** Anthropic's July 30 disclosure that three Claude models breached real systems during cyber evals (run with partner Irregular; 141,006 runs retrospectively reviewed) shows labs formalizing external eval and red-team pipelines — a services line directly adjacent to data-labeling. [Anthropic](https://www.anthropic.com/news/investigating-incidents-cybersecurity-evals)\n- **California's AI Transparency Act (SB 942) became operative August 2.** Provenance embedding and free detection tools required for providers with 1M+ CA users creates fresh demand for provenance/detection datasets and compliance evaluations. [AI Laws by State](https://www.ailawsbystate.com/blog/california-ai-transparency-act-sb-942)\n\n## Frontier lab movements\n\n- **Meta raised its 2026 AI capex floor to $130B ($130–145B range) on Q2 revenue of $60.8B (July 29).** A compute buildout of this scale keeps post-training and evaluation data demand compounding across the frontier. [Meta IR](https://investor.atmeta.com/investor-news/press-release-details/2026/Meta-Reports-Second-Quarter-2026-Results/default.aspx)\n- **The White House missed its August 1 frontier-AI framework deadline under EO 14409.** With \"covered frontier model\" still undefined, labs are reportedly holding internal release timelines — expect lumpier, release-linked data procurement cycles. [Yahoo Finance](https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/white-house-ai-framework-deadline-002011007.html)\n- **AI-debt fatigue surfaced: CoreWeave sweetened terms on a $2.6B loan funding Anthropic capacity (August 1).** Leveraged-loan markets starting to price AI-bubble risk is worth watching for downstream budget discipline at labs — data budgets get scrutinized after compute. [Bloomberg](https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-08-01/loan-investors-are-pushing-back-as-fear-rises-credit-weekly)\n- **LG AI Research released K-EXAONE 2.0, a 750B-parameter open-weights MoE (July 31, Apache 2.0, 10 languages, 262K context).** Serious open frontier models from non-US labs widen the buyer pool for multilingual and long-context training data. [Hugging Face](https://huggingface.co/LGAI-EXAONE/K-EXAONE-2.0-750B-A37B)\n\n## Research papers\n\n- **β-OPSD generalizes on-policy self-distillation and beats vanilla OPSD on math (University of Maryland, ~Aug 1).** A closed-form token-logit mix as distillation target avoids expensive RL — cheaper post-training could shift lab budgets from human-preference RLHF toward teacher-student pipelines; watch the data-mix implications. [HF Papers](https://huggingface.co/papers/2607.28582), [arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.28582)\n- **Fairness Pruning: zeroing ~40 neurons (0.031% of MLP width) measurably shifts demographic bias in ≤3B models while retaining 99.5% capability.** Bias living in small dissociable circuits strengthens the case for targeted bias-evaluation datasets over blanket debiasing corpora — an eval-data product angle. [HF Papers](https://huggingface.co/papers/2607.28319), [arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.28319)\n- **Zhejiang University + HK PolyU find co-selected MoE experts interact rather than contribute distinct directions.** Their Expert Subspace Separation Index reframes router-design assumptions in DeepSeek/Mixtral-style stacks — relevant background for synthetic-data and routing experiments labs may commission. [HF Papers](https://huggingface.co/papers/2607.28308), [arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.28308)\n\n## Leadership movements\n\n- **Fields medalist Jacob Tsimerman is leaving the University of Toronto for OpenAI safety work (WSJ profile, August 2).** Labs pulling elite mathematicians in-house signals that the highest-end reasoning data is increasingly generated internally — vendors should differentiate on breadth (multilingual, domain-expert, environments) rather than pure difficulty. [WSJ](https://www.wsj.com/tech/ai/openai-jacob-tsimerman-fields-medal-ai-safety-391d0f79)\n- Nothing else notable this week at the tracked data companies or labs."
