    "markdown": "**Top of mind:** Big Tech's July 29 earnings confirmed the training buildout is still accelerating — Meta raised its 2026 AI capex floor to $130B and Microsoft's Azure crossed $100B for the fiscal year — the clearest signal yet that the lab budgets funding human-data spend are not contracting. Meanwhile the end-of-July close window Bloomberg reported for Mercor's $500M raise at a $20B valuation expires today with still no confirmation from the company.\n\n## Competitor moves\n\n- **Mercor's reported end-of-July window to close its $500M round at a $20B valuation expires today, with no confirmation from the company or investors.** Bloomberg reported on July 9 that at least one term sheet was in and the deal was expected to close \"later this month\"; as of July 30 nothing has been announced. If it slips into August, expect scrutiny of whether the March LiteLLM breach and Meta's paused work weighed on terms. [Bloomberg](https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-07-09/ai-training-startup-mercor-discusses-20-billion-valuation), [Forbes](https://www.forbes.com/sites/richardnieva/2026/07/09/mercor-fundraise/)\n- **No other verifiable fresh news in the last 48 hours on Scale AI, Surge AI, Turing, Handshake AI, Deccan AI, Labelbox, Appen or Invisible.** Scale AI logged zero tracked stories this week in AI Weekly's entity index — unusually quiet for the category leader. [AI Weekly](https://aiweekly.co/ai-news-today)\n\n## New projects & opportunities\n\n- **IndiaAI Mission will back 20 sovereign AI models — 12 LLMs and 8 SLMs — IT Minister Ashwini Vaishnaw announced on July 23.** Every one of those funded model teams will need Indic-language corpora, instruction data, RLHF and evaluation, a domestic pipeline opportunity for India-based data vendors to lock in before global players position themselves. [CXOToday](https://cxotoday.com/governance/indiaai-mission-set-to-support-20-sovereign-ai-models/), [IndiaAI](https://indiaai.gov.in/)\n- **Recursive Superintelligence — Richard Socher's new lab — signed a multiyear $400M AWS compute contract on July 28 and says first products ship by October 2026.** A freshly funded lab building \"open-ended self-improving systems\" and prioritizing \"agent count over headcount\" is a new prospective buyer for RL environments, agent evals and expert demonstration data. [TechCrunch](https://techcrunch.com/2026/07/28/recursive-superintelligence-signs-400-compute-deal-with-amazon/)\n- **The EU formally opened bidding for seven AI gigafactories on July 30 — €10B public funding, ~€30B with private capital, bids due November 12.** A European sovereign-compute wave implies a European sovereign-model wave behind it, and with it demand for multilingual EU-language training data and evaluation. [AP via News4Jax](https://www.news4jax.com/business/2026/07/30/eu-lays-out-114-billion-for-7-ai-gigafactories-as-it-aims-to-catch-up-with-us-and-china/)\n\n## Frontier lab movements\n\n- **Meta raised its 2026 AI capex range to $130B–$145B on Q2 revenue of $60.8B (+28% YoY).** Post-earnings capex hikes are the most reliable leading indicator that model-training programs — and the post-training human-data budgets attached to them — keep growing into 2027. [Meta IR](https://investor.atmeta.com/investor-news/press-release-details/2026/Meta-Reports-Second-Quarter-2026-Results/default.aspx)\n- **Microsoft's Azure grew 43% and crossed $100B for FY26; its filings also disclosed a $3.2B one-quarter gain on its Anthropic stake against a ~$600M OpenAI markdown.** Anthropic's valuation trajectory matters to data vendors directly — it is the customer whose training and eval budgets are compounding fastest. [Microsoft IR](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/Investor/earnings/FY-2026-Q4/press-release-webcast), [TechCrunch](https://techcrunch.com/2026/07/29/microsoft-logs-3-2b-from-anthropic-investment-but-openai-was-a-mixed-bag/)\n- **OpenAI claimed on July 30 that two Responses-API settings (Retained Reasoning and Compaction) lift GPT-5.6 Sol from 7.8% to 38.3% on ARC-AGI-3 — past Claude Opus 5's 30.2%; ARC's François Chollet accepted the result.** Benchmark outcomes now swing 5x on harness configuration, which strengthens the case labs will pay neutral third parties for standardized, harness-controlled evaluation. [The Decoder](https://the-decoder.com/openai-claims-gpt-5-6-sol-beats-opus-5-on-arc-agi-3-with-its-latest-api-and-two-additional-settings/)\n- **Dwarkesh Patel argued in a July 29 essay that AI compute could get 10–15x more expensive as lab revenue growth outpaces the ~3x annual compute build.** If compute becomes the scarce input, the premium shifts to data quality and sample efficiency — a structural tailwind for curated human data over brute-force scale. [Dwarkesh Patel](https://www.dwarkesh.com/p/why-compute-might-get-10x-more-expensive)\n\n## Research papers\n\n- **\"Shadow Evaluations\" (Kirgis, Kapoor et al., 25 authors): frontier agents given two unpublished NeurIPS 2026 submissions completed all engineering work autonomously but were \"unambiguously rejected\" on the research itself.** The five failure modes it identifies — publishability judgment, uncreative problem-solving, poor backtracking, weak resource awareness, instruction drift — are precisely what PhD-level human evaluation and demonstration data address; strong sales collateral for expert-eval offerings. [Hugging Face Papers](https://huggingface.co/papers/2607.27191)\n- **CoRT adds token-level credit assignment to GRPO via rubric-conditioned counterfactual replay, gaining an average 4.4 points over response-level GRPO with no auxiliary scorer.** As rubric-conditioned RL gets more effective, well-authored rubrics become a higher-value deliverable class for human-data vendors. [Hugging Face Papers](https://huggingface.co/papers/2607.25659)\n- **SecRespond (Alibaba-NLP): the first benchmark for LLM agents doing post-compromise incident response — none of 23 frontier LLMs fully solved any of its 10 cyber ranges.** Every published capability-gap benchmark seeds lab demand for expert trajectories and environments in that domain; security operations looks like the next one. [Hugging Face Papers](https://huggingface.co/papers/2607.26791)\n\n## Leadership movements\n\n- **Chris Lattner becomes EVP of Advanced AI Software at Qualcomm as its acquisition of Modular closed on July 29.** One of AI infrastructure's most-followed builders now sits inside a chipmaker chasing a $5B data-center revenue target — another sign of AI software talent consolidating into silicon vendors. [HPCwire](https://www.hpcwire.com/aiwire/2026/07/29/qualcomm-completes-acquisition-of-modular/)\n- **Geoffrey Hinton and Yann LeCun joined the advisory board of Max Welling's CuspAI, per an FT interview published July 30.** Adjacent to our space rather than in it, but materials/science foundation models are a domain where expert-generated and simulation data is the bottleneck — worth tracking as a future buyer category. [FT](https://www.ft.com/content/5c2ae092-14af-4bd1-8e3d-8996755cba6a)\n- **Nothing verifiable in the last 48 hours at Scale AI, Surge AI, Turing, Mercor, Handshake or the frontier labs' data organizations.**"
